  "description": "The DITRDCSA Data Catalogue is the Australian Government Department of Infrastructure, Transport, Regional Development, Communications, Sport and the Arts' curated entry point to Australian infrastructure, regional and transport data, run on the CKAN platform with an open API. On 2026-09-29 it listed 449 dataset records in three groups: National Freight Data (224, the National Freight Data Hub), the Regional Data Hub (154) and Road Safety Data (71, linked to the National Road Safety Hub). Most records point to data held by others: the Bureau of Infrastructure and Transport Research Economics (BITRE, 116 records), the Australian Bureau of Statistics (33), the Department itself (45), and state and territory road and transport agencies such as Transport for NSW, VicRoads, Queensland Transport and Main Roads, Main Roads WA and the South Australian Department for Infrastructure and Transport. Examples are the Australian Road Deaths Database, ANCAP safety ratings, state roadworks and traffic feeds, freight commodity reports, land transport pricing, air traffic statistics, the Infrastructure Investment Program and regional census indicators. Coverage is Australia, from national down to local government area and statistical area level 2; records span 1991 onward and the newest was changed on 2026-09-29. Formats are mostly HTML landing pages and PDF or report files, with some CSV, XLSX, GeoJSON and API endpoints. Access is free. Licence is set per dataset: about 215 records name a Creative Commons Attribution licence and 143 state no licence, so check each record before reuse. It serves freight network, road safety and regional demand modelling by locating the source dataset. Related records: BITRE heavy vehicle median speed, the Australian national roads layer and the Digital Atlas of Australia.",
